    "text": "Verify that self-aligned double patterning (SADP) combined with high-NA EUV can simultaneously meet critical dimension uniformity and overlay error budgets for all logic layers at target design rules below 7 nm, without requiring field stitching in any layer.",
    "topic": "Logic SADP process window without stitching"
  },
  {
    "text": "Measure the depth of focus and exposure latitude for DRAM storage node contacts printed with central obscuration illumination at pitches ≤30 nm, and confirm that the process window is sufficient across the entire full-field area without stitching.",
    "topic": "DRAM single-exposure depth of focus"
  },
  {
    "text": "Determine whether innovative layout decomposition (e.g., mask shifting or non-critical-area stitching) can fully avoid at-resolution field stitching in logic chips while maintaining overlay and edge placement error margins.",
    "topic": "Layout strategy for logic stitching avoidance"
  },
  {
    "text": "Quantify the edge placement error and process window of stitching-free high-NA EUV approaches versus existing DUV multi-patterning for logic and DRAM, to assess feasibility at required yields.",
    "topic": "Comparative yield assessment stitching-free vs DUV"
  }
]
